// UART console IPC API.
//
// One operation: send bytes. The driver blocks the caller until the
// whole lease has been pushed into the TX FIFO (spinning politely when
// the FIFO is nearly full), so a returned Ok means "handed to the
// hardware", not "on the wire". There is no read operation yet: received
// bytes are echoed by the driver as a bring-up affordance, and a real
// console protocol replaces that when something needs input.

Interface(
    name: "Uart",
    ops: {
        "write": (
            args: {},
            leases: {
                "source": (type: "[u8]", read: true, max_len: Some(1024)),
            },
            reply: Result(
                ok: "()",
                err: ServerDeath,
            ),
        ),
    },
)
